{{- /*
Targets chezmoi deletes on apply. Kept permanently: applying is idempotent
(nothing to delete once gone) and the list documents what this repo used to own.

chezmoi has no `apply --prune` (verified on 2.73.2), so without an entry here a
renamed or removed *managed* file stays on disk forever — e.g. a renamed
~/.config/zsh/common fragment would keep being sourced, silently loading stale
config.

IMPORTANT: an entry is ignored if the same path is also in .chezmoiignore — the
ignore wins and nothing is removed (verified). The other OS's fragment directory
is ignored by .chezmoiignore.tmpl, so it must be cleaned once by hand instead:
    Linux:  rm -rf ~/.config/zsh/darwin
    macOS:  rm -rf ~/.config/zsh/linux

Example entry (one path per line):
.config/zsh/common/99-something-renamed.zsh
*/ -}}

